🎙️🌍🌱 This summer, I was invited to appear on the Kaleiodoscience podcast to present my recent work in environmental psychology. This podcast, launched by a bunch of psychologists from Germany, invites a cognitive science researcher to each episode to discuss their research, with the goal of making research accessible to a general audience. It’s a commendable project. It’s not something we’re exposed to enough in research, even though it’s important. 
<br><br>
I was a little nervous at the start of the interview, but the conversation flowed smoothly and was very enriching. Thank you for all your insightful questions and comments, for all your hard work, and for the invitation! 🙏
<br><br>
🎧 For those who are interested, you can find this episode <a href="https://open.spotify.com/episode/0QPZRG9zTBDZrc0dVQMbh0?si=v5mmeS48RUKYiXP7NK91oQ&utm_source=copy-link" target="_blank"> here</a> on Spotify. 

